  ### 🎯 Exercise 09: Manipulate BGP Paths using Weight Attribute via Route Maps

- If we want to go to 51.51.51.51 we use ISP1:CONVERGE(208.8.8.4)
- If we want to go to 52.52.52.52 we use ISP2:PLDT(207.7.7.2)
- If we want to go to 53.53.53.53 we use ISP3:GLOBE(209.9.9.3)

!@R1
conf t
access-list 51 permit host 51.51.51.51
access-list 53 permit host 53.53.53.53
!

route-map ISPfor51 permit 10
 match ip address 51
 set weight 51
route-map ISPfor51 permit 20
!
route-map ISPfor53 permit 10
 match ip address 53
 set weight 53
route-map ISPfor53 permit 20
!

router bgp 1
 neighbor 208.8.8.4 route-map ISPfor51 in
 neighbor 209.9.9.3 route-map ISPfor53 in
end
clear ip bgp * soft


### 🎯 Exercise 10: Manipulate BGP Paths using Weight Attribute via Route Maps

- If we want to go to 54.54.54.54 we use ISP1:CONVERGE(208.8.8.4)
- If we want to go to 55.55.55.55 we use ISP3:GLOBE(209.9.9.3)

!@R1
conf t
access-list 54 permit host 54.54.54.54
access-list 55 permit host 55.55.55.55
!
route-map ISPfor54 permit 10
 match ip address 54
 set weight 54
route-map ISPfor54 permit 20
!
route-map ISPfor55 permit 10
 match ip address 55
 set weight 55
route-map ISPfor55 permit 20
!

router bgp 1
 neighbor 208.8.8.4 route-map ISPfor54 in
 neighbor 209.9.9.3 route-map ISPfor55 in
end
clear ip bgp * soft


conf t
router bgp 1
no neighbor 208.8.8.4 route-map ISPfor54 in
no neighbor 209.9.9.3 route-map ISPfor55 in


